    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S021",
      "patient_response": "Nice to meet you, Doc. Uh, well, they said I needed to come see you because... because my talking gets all mixed up lately. Like, I'll be trying to explain something simple, right? Like about the keys. I clean buildings, so I got this big ring of keys, heavy on the belt, and they jingle. Sounds just like a jail guard when I walk down the halls. \n\nWhich makes me think about the jail, and I try to explain about the jail to people, but then my mind just goes right over to... to this prayer rug. I saw a really beautiful prayer rug once, deep red, with these gold fringes on the end. And the patterns on it, they looked exactly like chess pieces. I don't even play chess much anymore, not since the ninth grade anyway. The knight is the tricky one because it jumps, you know? But I start talking about the prayer rug and the chess pieces, and... what was I saying? \n\nOh, right. Yeah, people just tell me they cannot follow what I am saying. They say I jump around too much.",
