    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been feeling unusually energetic, like you don't need much sleep, or have you been feeling extremely low or hopeless lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S036",
      "patient_response": "Well, energetic... yeah, I guess you could say that. I mean, I'll lay down for maybe two, three hours, tops. And then my eyes just pop open, way before the sun even thinks about coming up. I feel completely fresh, like I've slept a whole weekend. And I just start planning out all the things I need to do at work, mapping out the floors in my head. It's like sleep is just this thing other people need, you know? Not me. \n\nSpeaking of the sun coming up, though... have you ever really watched the sunrise from a high window? The building I clean, on the top floor, there's this one window facing east. And when the light hits the glass, it turns this crazy shade of orange. Not like a regular orange, but like the color of those old traffic cones they used to have back in the day. The really heavy rubber ones that smelled like tar if you got too close. I remember smelling tar when they were paving the street outside my house when I was a kid. The machines were so loud, rumbling the whole house... but yeah, I don't really need much sleep at all.",
