    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you ever feel like you are receiving special messages from things you see or hear, or do you ever hear voices that other people around you cannot hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Voices... yeah, actually. It's usually when I'm at work, late at night when the building's mostly empty. I'll be near the vents, or sometimes right by the mop closet on the third floor, and I'll hear this man's voice. He says my name, or he tells me I ruined everything. And Doc, it sounds as real as you sitting right there. It echoes a bit, you know? \n\nLike the way sound bounces around in an empty parking garage. I used to park my car in this underground garage downtown, back when I had that old Chevy. Man, that car was a boat. The suspension was shot, so every time you went over a speed bump, it felt like you were on a roller coaster. I loved roller coasters when I was a kid. The wooden ones, mostly. They rattle your teeth right out of your head, but there's something about the smell of the old wood and the grease on the tracks... \n\nAnyway, the voice. Yeah. It's just this man, telling me I ruined it all, clear as day.",
