    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have there been times in the past when you were sleeping normally and your mood was stable, yet you were still hearing these voices?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually. There have been times like that. Like, I remember a few weeks... maybe a month ago? I was sleeping fine, you know, a solid seven or eight hours. Wasn't feeling all revved up, wasn't feeling down in the dumps either. Just... normal, I guess. But I still heard him. For more than two weeks, I was still hearing that guy in the vents, telling me I ruined it. And I was also convinced the people working late in the offices were tapping on their desks to send signals about me. \n\nSpeaking of desks, some of these offices have those really nice, heavy mahogany ones. You don't see wood like that much anymore. It reminds me of this old cabinet my grandmother used to have in her dining room. She kept all her good china in there, the plates with the little blue flowers painted around the edges. We were never allowed to touch them, only on Thanksgiving. Thanksgiving was always a big deal at her house. The smell of the turkey roasting would hit you before you even opened the front door... but yeah, I was feeling totally fine mood-wise, sleeping regular, but still hearing the voice and seeing the signals for a couple of weeks there.",
